  "fixture_basis": [
    "Loader_Recipes_Ores:460-461 emits one legendary/exquisite/flawless gem when that form exists; ordinary 8/4/2 gem stacks are fallback arguments. Exact grade identity/count and existing chance arrays remain checked.",
    "Loader_Recipes_Ores:383,415-420 has purified ore plus eight fines: nine outputs and nine chances, not eight. Timing, EU, water amounts and four water variants remain checked.",
    "RecipeMapPrinter:135-149 produces printed pages, 512 ticks at 16 EU/t for ordinary books, 72 mB black dye and a retained data medium. Metadata/pages/material identity and no-dye/no-data/short-paper checks remain. GTMain manuals use source colored bound books rather than vanilla WRITTEN_BOOK only.",
    "Replicator admits ambient fluid outputs. Hydrogen produces 1000 mB registered gas with no item output; nucleon counts, QU duration and exact retained USB checks remain.",
    "DyeProcessingRecipes source dimensions: colors*(27+3*industrialCoolants)+26 flower rows+18 precursors+9 finishing rows. Only explicitly declared catalysts survive consumption. Heterogeneous fluid-output arrays are checked before indexing.",
    "Electronics source family dimensions are 168 fixed rows plus registered valid gem-group engravings (Ruby is one non-group row). Exact consumption, simulation immutability and three solder tier caps remain.",
    "Wood rows are checked one by one against GTWoodRecipes.CRAFT_ROWS (54 shaped/18 shapeless). Earlier 50 assumed cinnamon lacked four current source-backed log/beam rows; collision and non-mirror checks remain.",
    "Wire coverage includes old unpack/insulation plus wire_sizes source conversion recipes. Expected rows derive from registered family sizes/divisor guards, not observed count. Every row must match a permitted source selector slot and conserve conductor material/family.",
    "Standalone multiblock controllers use several source crafting providers; loaded crafting output identity is required, rather than membership in just MultiblockCraftingRecipes. Canonical copper packing/unpacking uses current material unification identity.",
    "Valid fuel recipes may have no item/fluid output: recognized fuel map plus negative EU/t and positive duration denotes energy output. Real input and ordinary processing output requirements remain.",
    "Reviewed Fe thermal source branch has no FURNACE target; preserve dust->144 mB molten iron in Smelter at 16 EU/t/830 ticks and existing 1:1 molten iron->wrought iron 16/16 route; reject invented generic Fe dust Melter route.",
    "Recovery first pass reported all six failing legacy inputs together: asphalt,cfoam,cfoam_fresh,cfoam_slab,concrete,concrete_reinforced. Followup checks fresh recovery, per-material conservation, unsafe inventory/worn-tool rejection and all 96 legacy/fixed color pairs with explicit cross-color rejection."
  ],
